# Sumit Narayan | Cybersecurity Portfolio

**Network Security · SOC & Blue Team · Industrial Cybersecurity**

Welcome to my cybersecurity portfolio. This repository documents my cybersecurity training, hands-on laboratory exercises, technical projects, and research in network defense, security operations, digital forensics, and industrial cybersecurity.

My objective is to develop practical cybersecurity capabilities while exploring how defensive security practices can strengthen the resilience of critical infrastructure.

## About Me

I am a security professional building technical expertise in cybersecurity through structured training, independent study, and practical laboratory work.

I am currently undertaking a **six-week Cybersecurity Training Programme at the Indian Institute of Technology Ropar (IIT Ropar)**. My previous learning includes Google Cybersecurity coursework, the **ISC2 Certified in Cybersecurity (CC)** certification, and a one-week cybersecurity course at the **Uttar Pradesh State Institute of Forensic Sciences**.

Alongside formal training, I undertake practical exercises through TryHackMe, Cisco Networking Academy, and controlled virtual lab environments.

My professional interests include network security, SOC and Blue Team operations, digital forensics, and the cybersecurity of industrial and maritime infrastructure.

## Core Areas of Interest

- **Network Security:** Network discovery, port scanning, protocol analysis, and traffic investigation.
- **SOC & Blue Team:** Security monitoring, log analysis, alert triage, and incident-response fundamentals.
- **Linux Security:** System administration, permissions, access control, and hardening.
- **Digital Forensics & Technical Analysis:** Evidence-oriented investigation, static binary analysis, and security-focused experimentation.
- **Industrial Cybersecurity:** IT/OT convergence, port cybersecurity, cyber-physical risk, and critical-infrastructure resilience.

