## Selected Projects & Labs

### Network Security & Traffic Analysis

- Network discovery and port scanning using Nmap and Zenmap.
- Examination of TCP/IP networking and common protocols.
- Wireshark packet-capture and traffic-analysis exercises.

[Explore Network Security Labs](network-labs/)

### Linux Security & Administration

- Linux file permissions and access-control exercises.
- Command-line investigation and system administration.
- Practical security configuration and troubleshooting.

### Reverse Engineering & Binary Analysis

- Static analysis of beginner-level password-validation binaries using Ghidra.
- Examination of program control flow, character comparisons, and ASCII arithmetic.
- Comparison of observed program behaviour with decompiled code.

### Web Security Laboratory

- Controlled web-security exercises using DVWA.
- Study of SQL injection concepts and application input validation.
- Documentation of test conditions, observations, and defensive lessons.

### Industrial & Maritime Cybersecurity

- Research on port cybersecurity and IT/OT convergence.
- Study of cyber-physical security risks in critical infrastructure.
- Analysis of maritime cyber incidents and relevant security guidance.

Project reports will distinguish completed practical work from ongoing study and proposed future exercises.

## Tools & Technologies

**Network analysis:** Nmap, Zenmap, Wireshark

**Operating systems:** Kali Linux, Ubuntu

**Technical analysis:** Ghidra, Linux command line, Bash, Python fundamentals

**Web security lab:** DVWA

**Networking concepts:** TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP, ARP, ports and protocols

Tools and concepts listed here reflect varying levels of hands-on exposure; this portfolio documents that progression transparently.

